IMPORT prelude

-- Infrastructure Protection Act 2017 (Singapore) -- entry to protected places and directions (ss 20-23), defensive measures and
-- compensation (s 25), the specified surrounding area and the officer's duty to show authority (ss 26, 27, 31), prohibited
-- photography, including by drone (ss 29, 30), security plans for special developments and what counts as specified works or a
-- major renovation (ss 2, 35, 36(3), 39), appeals (s 62), and the penalty, composition and bail provisions (ss 20-77, 74, 75).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IPA2017.txt. The deposit
-- labels itself "Informal Consolidation – version in force from 1/7/2025"; the latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 3 of
-- 2021 wef 01/07/2025 (s 28(3)); Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022 is annotated at s 77.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 7 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a member of the public, a building
-- owner or a developer meets. Not encoded: appointment of the Commissioner and officers (ss 5-7), the making, contents, notice,
-- amendment and revocation of protected area and place orders (ss 8-19), the inspection powers of s 28 beyond its penalty, special
-- infrastructures designated under s 41 and their duties (ss 41-48), the content of security directives (ss 49-55, 57), the content
-- of Minister's orders (ss 58, 59, 61), the Appeal Advisory Board (ss 63, 64), enforcement powers (ss 65-69), corporate and
-- partnership liability (ss 72, 73), confidentiality orders (s 77) beyond its penalty, and Part 9 generally.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Infrastructure Protection Act 2017 -- protection`

DECLARE Premises IS ONE OF
    `a protected area`
    `a protected place`

§§ `20 -- no unauthorised entry to a protected place`

-- s 20(1): "A person must not enter a protected place unless the person -- (a) has a permit issued by the authority of the protected
-- place; or (b) is permitted to enter the protected place by an authorised officer of the protected place who is on duty at the
-- protected place at that time." (2): $20,000 or 2 years or both. There is no equivalent bar on entering a protected AREA; entry to
-- an area is controlled by directions under s 21.
GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises, `entered` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a permit from the authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `permitted by an officer on duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry is an offence` IF
        `the premises` EQUALS `a protected place`
    AND `entered`
    AND (NOT `has a permit from the authority`)
    AND (NOT `permitted by an officer on duty`)

§§ `22 -- removal and arrest without warrant`

-- s 22(1): an authorised officer may remove, or arrest without warrant, a person who "(a) in the case of a protected area,
-- contravenes section 21(4); (b) in the case of a protected place, contravenes section 20(1) or 21(4); or (c) in the authorised
-- officer's opinion -- (i) does not have a good and lawful reason to enter or be in that protected area or that protected place;
-- or (ii) is acting in a suspicious manner."
GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises, `entered without permit or permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `disobeyed a direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `officer thinks no good and lawful reason` IS A BOOLEAN, `officer thinks acting suspiciously` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may remove or arrest` IF
        `disobeyed a direction`
    OR  (`the premises` EQUALS `a protected place` AND `entered without permit or permission`)
    OR  `officer thinks no good and lawful reason`
    OR  `officer thinks acting suspiciously`

§§ `23 -- deadly force on arrest`

-- s 23(1): applies to an arrest under s 22(2)(b) of a person who "(a) attempts to enter or is in a protected area or a protected
-- place; and (b) does not stop despite being directed to do so at least 3 times". (2): the force "may, if necessary to effect that
-- person's arrest, extend to the voluntary causing of that person's death."
GIVEN `arrest power arises` IS A BOOLEAN, `times directed to stop` IS A NUMBER, `stopped` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `necessary to effect the arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `force may extend to causing death` IF
        `arrest power arises`
    AND `times directed to stop` AT LEAST 3
    AND (NOT `stopped`)
    AND `necessary to effect the arrest`

§§ `25 -- defensive measures and no compensation`

-- s 25(1): the Minister may authorise measures "including defensive measures that involve or may involve danger to the life of a
-- person entering". (2): the authority must take reasonably necessary precautions "(including the prominent display of warning
-- notices)". (3): "Where the precautions ... are taken, no person is entitled to any compensation or damages for any injury
-- sustained or death caused as a result of any unauthorised entry".
GIVEN `measure authorised by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `precautions taken` IS A BOOLEAN, `entry was unauthorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compensation is barred` IF
    `measure authorised by the Minister` AND `precautions taken` AND `entry was unauthorised`

§§ `26, 27, 31 -- the specified surrounding area`

-- s 26(2): powers under ss 27 and 28 may be exercised in the specified surrounding area "(a) ... where the specified surrounding area
-- is a public place, at any time; and (b) in any other case, only with the consent of the owner or occupier".
GIVEN `the surrounding area is a public place` IS A BOOLEAN, `owner or occupier consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surrounding-area powers are exercisable` IF
    `the surrounding area is a public place` OR `owner or occupier consents`

-- s 27(4), (5): every person in the specified surrounding area must comply with a request (name, address, identity, reason) or a
-- written move-on direction; $20,000 or 2 years or both. s 31(1): the officer must "on demand ... produce ... evidence of the
-- authorised person's identity and authority"; (2): "it is not an offence for any person to refuse to comply" if the officer does
-- not. The same s 31 rule covers ss 28, 29 and 30.
GIVEN `power exercisable` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN, `demanded evidence of authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `officer produced it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to comply in the surrounding area is an offence` IF
        `power exercisable`
    AND `failed to comply`
    AND (NOT (`demanded evidence of authority` AND (NOT `officer produced it`)))

§§ `29 -- prohibited photography`

-- s 29(1): "A person must not take any photograph of a protected area or a protected place (whether from inside, outside or above
-- ...) without the permission of the authority". (5): taking a photograph includes "(a) the making of a film or a video recording;
-- (b) the making of a recording of an image for the purpose of broadcasting or live-streaming the image; and (c) the making of a
-- drawing, diagram, plan, model, map, measurement, sounding or survey." (4): $20,000 or 2 years or both.
DECLARE Recording IS ONE OF
    `a photograph`
    `a video`
    `a live-stream`
    `a sketch`
    `a map or plan`
    `a measurement or survey`

DECLARE Vantage IS ONE OF
    `from inside`
    `from outside the fence`
    `from above`

GIVEN `the recording` IS A Recording, `the vantage` IS A Vantage, `authority's permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recording is prohibited photography` IF
    NOT `authority's permission`

§§ `30 -- photography by unmanned aircraft`

-- s 30(4): if a photograph is taken without permission "using any equipment on board an unmanned aircraft while the unmanned aircraft
-- is in flight, the operator of the unmanned aircraft, and the person taking the photograph if the person is not the operator, shall
-- each be guilty". (6)(a): the prosecution need not prove the accused knew the premises was protected, or that the aircraft had
-- camera equipment; (b) "it is a defence ... to prove, on a balance of probabilities, that the photograph was not taken intentionally
-- but was taken because of weather conditions or other unavoidable cause."
GIVEN `photographed from a drone in flight without permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the operator or the person taking it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew the premises was protected` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved unintentional by weather or unavoidable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the drone photograph is an offence` IF
        `photographed from a drone in flight without permission`
    AND `is the operator or the person taking it`
    AND (NOT `proved unintentional by weather or unavoidable cause`)

§§ `2 -- specified works and major renovation`

-- s 2(1) "specified works": "(a) for a special development, means any works for or affecting the foundation, retaining structure,
-- substructure or superstructure of any building"; "(b) for a special infrastructure, means -- (i) any extension ...; (ii) any major
-- renovation ...; or (iii) any other type of works prescribed by the Minister".
-- "major renovation": "(a) in the case of any part of a building that contains a critical asset, or is a public place or is
-- otherwise accessible to vehicles or vessels, any alteration, extension, repair, dismantling or demolition works carried out to the
-- structure or glazing of that part; (b) any installation or relocation of a critical asset in the premises; or (c) any alteration,
-- extension, dismantling or demolition works affecting the perimeter of the premises".
DECLARE Works IS ONE OF
    `structural or glazing works`
    `installing or relocating a critical asset`
    `perimeter works`
    `other works`

GIVEN `the works` IS A Works, `part contains a critical asset` IS A BOOLEAN, `part is a public place` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `part accessible to vehicles or vessels` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the works are a major renovation` IF
    CONSIDER `the works`
    WHEN `structural or glazing works` THEN `part contains a critical asset` OR `part is a public place` OR `part accessible to vehicles or vessels`
    WHEN `installing or relocating a critical asset` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `perimeter works` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE BuildingWorks IS ONE OF
    `foundation works`
    `retaining structure works`
    `substructure works`
    `superstructure works`
    `interior decoration not affecting the structure`

-- Inference: works that affect none of the four named elements are not specified works for a special development under limb (a).
GIVEN `the works` IS A BuildingWorks
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the works are specified works for a special development` IF
    CONSIDER `the works`
    WHEN `interior decoration not affecting the structure` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `35, 36(3) -- security plan before works`

-- s 35(1): the responsible person "must not carry out, or cause or allow the carrying out of, any specified works ... unless the
-- responsible person has obtained ... the Commissioner's approval, or provisional approval, of a security plan". (2): $200,000 or
-- 2 years or both.
GIVEN `carries out specified works` IS A BOOLEAN, `plan approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `plan provisionally approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the works are an offence under s 35` IF
    `carries out specified works` AND (NOT `plan approved`) AND (NOT `plan provisionally approved`)

-- s 36(3): if a requirement to amend and resubmit "is not complied with within the time specified in the notice ..., or such
-- extended time as the Commissioner may give in writing, the application ... is, on the expiry of that time, treated as rejected".
GIVEN `resubmitted` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since the notice` IS A NUMBER, `days allowed in the notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `days of written extension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is treated as rejected` IF
    (NOT `resubmitted`) AND `days since the notice` GREATER THAN `days allowed in the notice` PLUS `days of written extension`

§§ `39 -- certificate of works completion`

-- s 39(2): the certificate must be submitted "(a) in the case where a temporary occupation permit is required ..., before obtaining
-- any temporary occupation permit; and (b) in any other case, within the prescribed time after completion". (4): "Any person who
-- contravenes subsection (2)(b) shall be guilty of an offence" -- $10,000. Subsection (2)(a) is not named in (4).
GIVEN `TOP required` IS A BOOLEAN, `submitted on time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the late certificate is an offence under s 39(4)` IF
    (NOT `TOP required`) AND (NOT `submitted on time`)

§§ `62 -- appeals to the Minister`

-- s 62(1): appeal lies against (a), (b) the Commissioner's rejection of a security plan or amended security plan, "within 14 days
-- after the rejection"; (c) a security directive issued by the Commissioner under Part 5, "within 14 days after the issue". (6):
-- "The Minister's decision on the appeal is final." No appeal is listed against a Minister's order under Part 6.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `rejection of a security plan`
    `rejection of an amended security plan`
    `security directive by the Commissioner`
    `provisional approval subject to conditions`
    `Minister's order under s 58`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `days after the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister lies` IF
        `days after the decision` AT MOST 14
    AND CONSIDER `the decision`
        WHEN `rejection of a security plan` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `rejection of an amended security plan` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `security directive by the Commissioner` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 62(4): "Unless otherwise directed by the Minister in any particular case, the Commissioner's decision being appealed against does
-- not take effect until the earlier of ... (a) the Minister determines the appeal; (b) the appellant withdraws the appeal."
GIVEN `appealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `determined or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is held in suspense` IF
    `appealed` AND (NOT `determined or withdrawn`) AND (NOT `Minister directed otherwise`)

§§ `penalties, 74 and 75 -- maximum punishment, composition and bail`

-- Penalty subsections as read: ss 20(2), 21(6), 27(5), 28(2), 29(4), 30(4), 70 -- $20,000 or 2 years; s 35(2) -- $200,000 or 2
-- years; s 37(7) -- $100,000 or 2 years, $2,500 a day continuing; s 39(4) -- $10,000 fine only; s 40(3) -- $20,000 or 2 years,
-- $1,000 a day; s 56(3)(a) (s 55 directive) -- $50,000 or 2 years, $2,500 a day; s 56(3)(b) (other directives) -- $100,000 or 2
-- years, $2,500 a day; s 60(3) (Minister's order) -- $100,000 or 5 YEARS, $2,500 a day; s 71 -- $20,000 or 2 years, $1,000 a day;
-- s 77(6) -- $10,000 fine only.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `entering a protected place`
    `disobeying an entry or conduct direction`
    `prohibited photography`
    `drone photography`
    `works without an approved security plan`
    `ignoring a notice to amend a security plan`
    `late certificate of works completion`
    `not maintaining security measures`
    `breaching a s 55 security directive`
    `breaching another security directive`
    `breaching a Minister's order`
    `false or misleading information`
    `obstruction`
    `publishing a protected document`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `works without an approved security plan` THEN 200000
    WHEN `ignoring a notice to amend a security plan` THEN 100000
    WHEN `late certificate of works completion` THEN 10000
    WHEN `breaching a s 55 security directive` THEN 50000
    WHEN `breaching another security directive` THEN 100000
    WHEN `breaching a Minister's order` THEN 100000
    WHEN `publishing a protected document` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `late certificate of works completion` THEN 0
    WHEN `publishing a protected document` THEN 0
    WHEN `breaching a Minister's order` THEN 5
    OTHERWISE 2

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further daily fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `ignoring a notice to amend a security plan` THEN 2500
    WHEN `breaching a s 55 security directive` THEN 2500
    WHEN `breaching another security directive` THEN 2500
    WHEN `breaching a Minister's order` THEN 2500
    WHEN `not maintaining security measures` THEN 1000
    WHEN `obstruction` THEN 1000
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 74(1): the Commissioner may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" for "a sum not exceeding the lower of ...
-- (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000." Which offences are prescribed is
-- left to regulations not deposited; this computes only the cap.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

-- s 75(1): every offence is arrestable. (2): every offence is bailable "except an offence under section 20(2), 21(6), 27(5), 28(2),
-- 29(4), 30(4) or (5), 37(7), 44(7), 56(3) or (4) or 60(3)".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is bailable` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `works without an approved security plan` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `late certificate of works completion` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `not maintaining security measures` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `false or misleading information` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `obstruction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `publishing a protected document` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
